# Compressed swap policy for uflinux-zram. Everything here is optional; the
# service computes its own defaults from the installed RAM and the CPU.

# Systems with at most this much RAM get zram only. Above it the service also
# creates a swapfile and turns on zswap, so that compressed pages can be
# written out instead of being pinned in RAM forever.
#RAM_SPLIT_MIB=4096

# Compression algorithm. Leave empty to choose from the CPU: lz4 on low-end
# machines (32-bit ARM, riscv64, or two cores or fewer) and zstd elsewhere.
# Both are built into the UFLinux kernels, so either name works; an unknown
# name makes the kernel keep its own default and the service only warns.
#ZRAM_COMP=""

# Size of the zram block device and the amount of real memory it may consume.
# Defaults: half of RAM clamped to 256 MiB..2048 MiB, and a quarter of RAM
# clamped to 64 MiB..1024 MiB. Suffixes such as 512M and 1G are accepted.
#ZRAM_DISKSIZE=1G
#ZRAM_MEM_LIMIT=512M

# Swapfile used as zswap's backing device on larger systems, its size, and the
# zswap pool limits. The default size is half of RAM clamped to
# 2048 MiB..8192 MiB. The file is created once, on first boot, with fallocate
# (or a full write on F2FS, which refuses a swapfile containing a hole).
#SWAPFILE=/swapfile
#SWAPFILE_MIB=4096
#ZSWAP_COMP="$ZRAM_COMP"
#ZSWAP_MAX_POOL_PERCENT=20
#ZSWAP_ACCEPT_THRESHOLD_PERCENT=70
